genic Cushing's syndrome the following are true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the commonest cause in adults is pituitary-dependent disease (true Cushing's disease)"},{"label":"B","text":"in the majority of patients with Cushing's disease the pituitary fossa on lateral skull x-ray appears normal"},{"label":"C","text":"hypokalaemia is more common in ectopic ACTH syndrome than Cushing's disease"},{"label":"D","text":"in Cushing's syndrome associated with bronchial carcinoma the classical physical findings are usually florid"},{"label":"E","text":"the skin may peel after succesful restoration of the eucorticoid state"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-47aa4cf40c5d","stem":"Laurence-Moon-Biedl syndrome is characterised by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"peripheral neuropathy"},{"label":"B","text":"obesity"},{"label":"C","text":"retinitis pigmentosa"},{"label":"D","text":"hyperlipaemia"},{"label":"E","text":"mental retardation"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_a