":"Accumulation of lactic acid is a recognised phenomenon in","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"myocardial infarction"},{"label":"B","text":"acute ethanol poisoning"},{"label":"C","text":"chlorpropamide treatment"},{"label":"D","text":"type I glycogenosis (von Gierke's disease)"},{"label":"E","text":"chronic renal failure"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-5440680f2a39","stem":"In myelofibrosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"a leuco-erythroblastic peripheral blood picture is a characteristic finding"},{"label":"B","text":"there may be a preceding history of polycythaemia"},{"label":"C","text":"the Philadelphia chromosome can be demonstrated in the majority of cases"},{"label":"D","text":"gout is a recognised complication"},{"label":"E","text":"electrophoresis of the serum would be expected to show a characteristic band in the gamma-globulin zone"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","au