sociation can be seen"},{"label":"C","text":"the QRS complexes are very wide"},{"label":"D","text":"the rhythm is irregularly irregular"},{"label":"E","text":"P waves are seen following each QRS complex"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-876522789923","stem":"The following are features of Fallot's tetralogy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"prominent systolic murmur of ventricular septal defect"},{"label":"B","text":"pulmonary plethora"},{"label":"C","text":"squatting"},{"label":"D","text":"paradoxical embolus"},{"label":"E","text":"presentation in late teens"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-11971721ee13","stem":"The following are recognised causes of reversible dilated cardiomyopathy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"alcohol"},{"label":"B","text":"Selenium deficiency"},{"label":"C","text":"Acromegaly"},{"label":"D","text":"Lead poisoning"},{"label":"E","text":"Coxsackie virus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-1b42cabff524","stem":"The following are true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"up to 25% of normal hearts have a patent foramen ovale"},{"label":"B","text":"left axis deviation on the ECG suggests an ostium secundum atrial septal defect"},{"label":"C","text":"ostium primum atrial septal defect is associated with mitral regurgitation"},{"label":"D","text":"appearence of a tricuspid flow murmur in a patient with an atrial septal defect suggests the development of the Eisenmenger complex"},{"label":"E","text":"anomalous pulmonary venous drainage is seen with a sinus venosus atrial septal defect"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"],"duplicateStemGroup":"c8509cb2aaf73bf52639fdc90b2b5c669f6a6baf"},{"id":"q-0c37d5ab4024","stem":"The following are true of atrial fibrillation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Digoxin is of use in the prevention of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation."},{"label":"B","text":"It is often not possible to give DC cardioversion because of the irregularity of the QRS complexes."},{"label":"C","text":"It is essential to continue giving warfarin for four weeks after successful DC cardioversion."},{"label":"D","text":"Treatment with sotalol may cause torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia."},{"label":"E","text":"Propafenone should be avoided in severe chronic obstructive airways disease."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-c3720e00034e","stem":"The following are true of cardiac transplantation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the donor heart is provided to the recipient with the best HLA match"},{"label":"B","text":"long term hypotension is a problem"},{"label":"C","text":"recipients suffer less angina but accelerated coronary artery disease"},{"label":"D","text":"the histology of atheroma in the transplanted heart is the same as that of typical atherosclerosis"},{"label":"E","text":"75% 5 year survival"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-9cbe720eea56","stem":"The following are true of coronary artery anatomy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Right bundle branch block in acute anterior myocardial infarction suggests obstruction prior to the first septal branch of the left anterior descending coronary artery"},{"label":"B","text":"the posterior descending artery is usually a branch of the circumflex artery"},{"label":"C","text":"The sinus node is supplied by a branch of the right coronary in over 90% of subjects."},{"label":"D","text":"The AV node is supplied by the left anterior descending coronary artery."},{"label":"E","text":"The left main stem is about 4 cm long"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-9d3b6eedb3b5","stem":"The following are true of infective endocarditis in intravenous drug abusers","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Staphylococcus albus is the commonest infecting organism"},{"label":"B","text":"the aortic valve is affected most often"},{"label":"C","text":"pulmonary abscess is a recognised association"},{"label":"D","text":"blood cultures may be negative in untreated disease"},{"label":"E","text":"murmurs are frequently absent"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-bbc5ba38e083","stem":"The following are true of Wolff-Parkinson-White related tachycardias","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"QRS alternans suggests a diagnosis of orthodromic atrioventricular reciprocating tachycardia (AVRT)"},{"label":"B","text":"antidromic AVRT is commoner than orthodromic AVRT"},{"label":"C","text":"orthodromic tachycardia may have wide QRS morphology"},{"label":"D","text":"the treatment of choice for atrial fibrillation with ventricular pre-excitation is digoxin"},{"label":"E","text":"adenosine is useful for terminating orthodromic AVRT"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-303b5d51fa6b","stem":"The following associations are true in patients who drink alcohol","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"cephamandole and facial flushing"},{"label":"B","text":"verapamil and prolonged intoxication"},{"label":"C","text":"methotrexate and reduced risk of hepatic dysfunction"},{"label":"D","text":"moclobemide and hypertensive crisis"},{"label":"E","text":"chlorpropamide and facial flushing"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-854b18cff11b","stem":"The following conditions are inherited as an autosomal dominant trait","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Friedrich's ataxia"},{"label":"B","text":"Ehlers-Danlos syndrome"},{"label":"C","text":"Noonan's syndrome"},{"label":"D","text":"Romano-Ward syndrome"},{"label":"E","text":"Marfan's syndrome"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-6d9dbbf3a409