ation of Barrett's oesophagus"},{"label":"D","text":"chest pain is a late symptom"},{"label":"E","text":"is a complication of coeliac disease"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-11990b6a8dfb","stem":"There is an increased risk of oesophageal cancer with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"coeliac disease"},{"label":"B","text":"oesophageal web"},{"label":"C","text":"excessive alcohol ingestion"},{"label":"D","text":"achalasia"},{"label":"E","text":"chronic gastric reflux"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-9e2c28c09db8","stem":"Familial hepatic diseases associated with cirrhosis include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","topicOriginal":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","subtopic":"Hepat","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"galactosaemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Osler-Weber-Rendu syndrome"},{"label"