iltrating the gastric mucosa"},{"label":"E","text":"is associated with gastric lymphoma"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"],"duplicateStemGroup":"4ffdec3eec8b8ae569af50b5772e3729b56bea2c"},{"id":"q-1f89c807fc3b","stem":"In a IIIrd nerve palsy there is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"ptosis"},{"label":"B","text":"a constricted pupil"},{"label":"C","text":"a convergent squint"},{"label":"D","text":"increased lacrimation"},{"label":"E","text":"enophthalmos"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-c8e7f9da1731","stem":"The following are true regarding papillary carcinoma of the thyroid gland.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Head and Neck","options":[{"label":"A","text":"is the most common cause of thyroid malignancy"},{"label":"B","text":"20% of cases have hypercalcaemia"},{"label":"C","text":"after destruction of the normal thyroid tissue by tumour there is