jor organs affected by visceral leishmaniasis or kalar azar?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Psychiatry","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Psychiatry","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6301c5d48227","stem":"Explain in detail how this happen.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7c474e15354e","stem":"Write short notes on","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Helminths parasite of lungs"},{"label":"B","text":"Diagnosis and pathology of ascariasis"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"0de5f4210f5edfaf2b6fe64d464684e183c7a46b"},{"id":"q-235566755cf9","stem":"Transmission of Giardia lamblia (4 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"-Fecal oral route (1) -Person-person transmission occurs by hand to mouth transfer of cysts from feces of an infected individual especially in institutions and daycare centres (1) - Ingestion of cysts in fecally contaminated water (1) - Vegetables can be contaminated from fertilizer made from human excreta or by food handler in the market (1)"},{"label":"B","text":"(4 marks) -Diarrhea is the main symptoms, usually offensive and with pale, almost white stools, but without blood or pus.(1) -Weakness and abdominal pain, nausea, anorexia and failure to thrive in children are important symptoms.(1) - Dyspepsia with giardia infection resembles hepatic disfunction with dull upper epigastric pain and nausea.(1) - Malabsorption of fats or fat-soluble vitamins may occur (1)"},{"label":"C","text":"Toxoplasma gondii (2)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9e22c4c4fc43","stem":"Describe biological aspects of Anopheles gambiae complex including: • Classification • Distribution • Breeding habits • Feeding and resting habits • Gonotrophic cycle","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":