cludes a chancre"},{"label":"C","text":"In Trypanosoma brucei gambiaense diseases Winterbottom’s sign is a Common local sign"},{"label":"D","text":"The incubation period is longer for Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense than for Trypanosoma brucei gambiaense"},{"label":"E","text":"Patient with Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense are commonly encountered by active case detection"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ecfbb73c9107","stem":"All of the following are true about Post Kala-azar Dermal Leishmaniasis except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Leishmaniasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prevalent in India, China and East Africa"},{"label":"B","text":"Sequela to antmony treatment failure"},{"label":"C","text":"Caused by Lesihamnia mexicana Mexicana"},{"label":"D","text":"Verrucous condition in the skin"},{"label":"E","text":"Caused by Leishmania donovani"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"9ac6cc8e316dd81f086e3850851ae534aa367116","manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-7f222091b940","stem":"Regarding the epidemiology of human African trypanosomiasis, the following statements are true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Trypanosomiasis","suggestedTo