inal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Immunity involves both humoral and cellular immunity"},{"label":"B","text":"Initially IgM antibodies develop and after 2 month there is a switch to IgC antibodies that probably persist for life."},{"label":"C","text":"In principle, high Igm titres indicate previous infection"},{"label":"D","text":"The humoral antibodies clear endozoites in pseudocysts"},{"label":"E","text":"Persistence of cytozoites in tissdue cysts creates a state of continuous immune activation"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a25f9c6c6892","stem":"Regarding the life cycle of human African trypanosomes, the following statement are true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Trypanosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The infective stages to man are the metacyclinc non-dividing trypomastigotes"},{"label":"B","text":"Both male and female Glossina transmit human African trypaosomes"},{"label":"C","text":"The short stumpu non-dividing trypomastigotes are the infective stages to Glossina"},{"label":"D","text":"Antigenic variation typically occurs when trypomastigotes have lost the surface coat."},{"label":"E","text":"Trypanosoma brucei rhodensiense is adapted to animals whiel Trypanosoma brucei gambiense is adapted to man."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unv