rasitize other RBCs.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-cd53260c75a9","stem":"When a parasite enters a foreign host, which of the following does not take places?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Immediate death of the parasite"},{"label":"B","text":"The parasite may be passed out unchanged"},{"label":"C","text":"The parasite survives for sometime but does not multiply"},{"label":"D","text":"The parasite develops to maturity but may or may not cause disease"},{"label":"F","text":"Parasite always confines itself to an abnormal site"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9d8c9ea81cb8","stem":"The following statements on the clinical features or African human trypanosomiasis are true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Trypanosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trypanosoma brucei rhodensiense dieases take an acute course while Trypanosoma gambiense takes a chronic course."},{"label":"B","text":"In Trypanosom brucei rhodesiense disease the local symtom includes a chancre."},{"label":"C","text":"In Trypanosoma brucei gambiense disease Winterbottom’s sign is a pathognomonic local sign."},{"label":"D","text":"Patients with encephalitic stage are commonly encountered in T.b. rhodesiense disease than in T.b. gambiense."},{"label":"E","text":"The incubation period of Trypanosoma brucei gambiense ranges from few weeks to the several months while in Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense, it is only few weeks."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-31ebf7e2a16b","stem":"The pathological changes involving the central nevous system are more typical of infection with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trypanosoma brucei brucei"},{"label":"B","text":"Trypanosoma brucei gambianse"},{"label":"C","text":"Trypanosoma brucei rhodensiense"},{"label":"D","text":"Trypanosoma conglense"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d8db7e1edd76","stem":"Regarding the epidemiology of human African tryopanosomiasis, the following statements are true except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ambulatory human carriers for both Trypanosoma brucei rhodesiense and T.b. gambiense serve as a resevoir of infection to tsetse flies"},{"label":"B","text":"Only T.b. rhodensiense is a zoonosis with wild animal reservoirs and domestic ungulates"},{"label":"C","text":"In Trypanosoma brucei gambiense the transmission cycle involves human-fly human"},{"label":"D","text":"Certain occupation including hunting, fishing, burning charcoal, pose a special risk."},{"label":"E","text":"Human African trypanosomiasis is an important differential diagnosis of fever in tourists returning from East Africa after touring national parks."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6b0836ef5b96","stem":"Naegleria fowleri,a free living amoeba is associated with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Granulomatous amoebic encephalitis"},{"label":"B","text":"Warm fresh water in which the biflagellated form is found"},{"label":"C","text":"Non-purulent CSF with absence of bacteria"},{"label":"D","text":"Feature of pyogenic meningitis minus neck rigidity"},{"label":"E","text":"Aerosol transmission."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3a59212bde82","stem":"Acanthamoeba spp is associated with","type":"Singl